The first symbolic run reached the loop base case, so the control-flow invariant is shaped correctly. It exposed one proof-engineering issue: the supplied `seqConcat` recurses on its left argument and cannot simplify the true identity `seqConcat(A, .IntSeq) = A` when `A` is symbolic. I’m replacing the spec’s direct recursive map with an equivalent accumulator definition whose base case is definitional, avoiding any added algebraic axiom.
