Concrete LLVM execution has now completed successfully for all four prompt examples, empty input, wraparound, and the full alphabet (`<k> .K </k>`, `NoExc`, exit code 0). I also identified why the composed proof is slow: the proved loop summary currently competes at the same rewrite priority as the ordinary one-step loop semantics, so the prover explores both. I’m raising only the summary’s priority in the composition definition; this does not affect the separate proof of that summary.
